A style rule without selectors, as a half-edited file has (`{ color: red }`), isn't listed, at
the top level or inside an at-rule, because its outline line would be blank; the rules around
it are listed as usual.
== args
input/broken.css
== file input/broken.css
{ color: red }
.a { color: blue }
@media print {
  { color: black }
  .b { color: gray }
}
== stdout
input/broken.css (6 lines)
[L2-L2] .a
[L3-L6] @media print
  [L5-L5] .b
== stderr
== exit 0
